:name: HEIMAN HS1SA (EFR32MG21) — ZB-06 emulation
:description: Boots the Heiman HS1SA smoke-detector Zigbee firmware on an emulated BRD4180A (EFR32MG21A020F1024IM32) for emulation-based vulnerability validation (mfg 0x120B/0xF3 record-count overflow in sub_1662e).

using sysbus
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution true
emulation CreateIEEE802_15_4Medium "wireless"

mach create "hs1sa"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/silabs/brd4180a.repl

$bin?=@scripts/silabs-vuln/hs1sa.elf

# NOTE: this application ELF is stripped (no __Vectors symbol). It is a Gecko
# app image loaded at flash 0x6000; its vector table is at the load base, so
# point VTOR there and let the Cortex-M load the initial SP/PC from it on reset.
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x6000
"""
runMacro $reset

# Radio into the shared 802.15.4 medium
connector Connect sysbus.radio wireless

# VCOM console (USART0) for firmware logs / CLI
showAnalyzer usart0

logLevel 2
